2. Use the taught procedure; expect a reasoned numeric or simplified-ratio/expression answer involving 11, 0, or 29. Teacher checks method + units.
3. Use the taught procedure; expect a reasoned numeric or simplified-ratio/expression answer involving 13, -1, or 10. Teacher checks method + units.
4. Use the taught procedure; expect a reasoned numeric or simplified-ratio/expression answer involving 7, 0, or 23. Teacher checks method + units.
5. Use the taught procedure; expect a reasoned numeric or simplified-ratio/expression answer involving 9, 7, or 44. Teacher checks method + units.
6. Use the taught procedure; expect a reasoned numeric or simplified-ratio/expression answer involving 11, 5, or 25. Teacher checks method + units.

</details>

## Exit ticket

1. In one sentence, what does “Unit Rates” let you do that you could not do as clearly before?
2. Name the common mistake to avoid today (hint: related to calling a non-statistical question ''statistical'' because…).
3. Create one new practice item (with answer) a classmate could try in 2 minutes.

*(Scored exit items also appear as multiple-choice checks below the lesson in Prosper Prep.)*

