2. Use the taught procedure; expect a reasoned numeric or simplified-ratio/expression answer involving 9, 2, or 25. Teacher checks method + units.
3. Use the taught procedure; expect a reasoned numeric or simplified-ratio/expression answer involving 11, 1, or 46. Teacher checks method + units.
4. Use the taught procedure; expect a reasoned numeric or simplified-ratio/expression answer involving 13, 0, or 27. Teacher checks method + units.
5. Use the taught procedure; expect a reasoned numeric or simplified-ratio/expression answer involving 15, 6, or 48. Teacher checks method + units.
6. Use the taught procedure; expect a reasoned numeric or simplified-ratio/expression answer involving 8, 5, or 29. Teacher checks method + units.

</details>

## Exit ticket

1. In one sentence, what does “Equations & Inequalities Mistakes” let you do that you could not do as clearly before?
2. Name the common mistake to avoid today (hint: related to doing operations left-to-right while ignoring parentheses…).
3. Create one new practice item (with answer) a classmate could try in 2 minutes.

