<summary>Answer key (teacher / self-check — try first before expanding)</summary>

1. Use the taught procedure; expect a reasoned numeric or simplified-ratio/expression answer involving 3, 10, or 16. Teacher checks method + units.
2. Use the taught procedure; expect a reasoned numeric or simplified-ratio/expression answer involving 5, 9, or 37. Teacher checks method + units.
3. Use the taught procedure; expect a reasoned numeric or simplified-ratio/expression answer involving 7, 8, or 18. Teacher checks method + units.
4. Use the taught procedure; expect a reasoned numeric or simplified-ratio/expression answer involving 10, 9, or 31. Teacher checks method + units.
5. Use the taught procedure; expect a reasoned numeric or simplified-ratio/expression answer involving 12, 8, or 12. Teacher checks method + units.
6. Use the taught procedure; expect a reasoned numeric or simplified-ratio/expression answer involving 14, 14, or 33. Teacher checks method + units.

</details>

## Exit ticket

1. In one sentence, what does “Surface Area vs Volume” let you do that you could not do as clearly before?
2. Name the common mistake to avoid today (hint: related to calling a non-statistical question ''statistical'' because…).
