3. Problem 3: Apply “Dot Plots” with quantities 12, 13, and 31 in a short story about a family road trip on I-20. Show work.
4. Problem 4: Apply “Dot Plots” with quantities 11, 14, and 18 in a short story about a Saturday soccer tournament. Show work.
5. Problem 5: Apply “Dot Plots” with quantities 11, 9, and 37 in a short story about a band concert ticket table. Show work.
